he worktree (`executor.Job.Scrub`), so a copy left from an earlier stage or run is never trusted. A role file the agent never wrote again fails the job (`role file not written by this job`, or `role file missing` when none was ever there). One it wrote again with identical bytes still counts, but only because the executor recorded the scrub in the handle (`Handle.Scrubbed`); close-out refuses an unscrubbed, unchanged role file (`role file not scrubbed by executor`). A non-zero exit fails the job even when a role file exists, and a failed job commits only its redacted log, never a partial `plan.md`.\n326:4. **The agent writes `review-<role>.md`** with `verdict: approve | changes` and `findings:` (`file`, `line`, `severity`, `blocking`, `message`; see the .ard/ contract). It may write nothing else under `.ard/<issue#>/`, and code edits are never collected. An `approve` that carries a blocking finding is treated as `changes` (the job succeeds and the comment says so).\n438:- **Agents write only their own files.** Close-out lets a job change under `.ard/<issue#>/` only its own role file and what its role owns (a `plan.md` section, `design/`); anything else fails the job as `needs-human` and is not committed (see the `.ard/` contract).\n\nfunc hasControl(s string) bool {\n\tfor _, r := range s {\n\t\tif unicode.IsControl(r) {\n\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false\n}\n\nfunc validateFinding(f Finding) error {\n\tswitch {\n\tcase f.Fingerprint == \"\":\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"fingerprint is required\")\n\tcase len(f.Fingerprint) > MaxFingerprint:\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"fingerprint longer than %d bytes\", MaxFingerprint)\n\tcase !utf8.ValidString(f.Fingerprint) || hasControl(f.Fingerprint):\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"fingerprint %q is not valid UTF-8 without control characters\", f.Fingerprint)\n\tcase strings.TrimSpace(f.Title) == \"\":\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"title is required\")\n\tcase utf8.RuneCountInString(f.Title) > MaxTitleRunes:\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"