{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X1yy71hieKBvFBayzHHrHK","type":"tool_result","content":"18:def globbody:\n97:    title: (\"`\\(.key)` \" + $title),\n100:    files: (.value | map(.p) | unique | .[:20]),\n101:    body: ($sentence + \"\\n\\nLocations:\\n\\n```text\\n\" + (.value | locs) + \"\\n```\\n\")\n  | .manifest as $m\n  | .package as $pkg\n  | . as $v\n  | {\n      fingerprint: (\"osv:\" + $canon + \":\" + $m + \":\" + $pkg),\n      title: (\"`\" + ($pkg | gsub(\"[`\\\\r\\\\n]\"; \"\")) + \"`: \" + $canon + \" (\" + $sev + \")\" | .[:200]),\n      severity: $sev,\n      group: $m,\n      files: [$m],\n      body: ([\n        \"Installed: \" + (if $v.installed == null then \"unknown\" else \"`\" + ($v.installed | safetxt) + \"`\" end),\n        \"Fixed in: \" + (if ($v.fixed | length) == 0 then \"none\" else ($v.fixed | map(\"`\" + safetxt + \"`\") | join(\", \")) end),\n        \"Reachable: \" + (if $v.reach == \"no\" then \"no (severity capped at medium)\" else $v.reach end),\n        \"Reported by: \" + ($v.tools | join(\", \")),\n        (if $v.toolchain == null then empty\n         else \"Go toolchain: `\" + ($v.toolchain | safetxt) + \"` (selected from go.mod; standard library findings are measured against it)\" end),\n        \"\",\n        \"Advisory summary (untrusted text from the advisory database):\",\n        \"```text\",\n        (($v.summary // \"(none)\") | gsub(\"`{3,}\"; \"'''\") | .[:500]),\n        \"```\",\n        \"\",\n        \"Advisories:\",\n        ($v.ids | map(safeid) | .[]\n          | \"- [\" + . + \"](https://osv.dev/vulnerability/\" + . + \")\"\n            + (if startswith(\"GHSA-\") then \" ([GitHub](https://github.com/advisories/\" + . + \"))\" else \"\" end))\nOnly in internal/roles/scanners/cve: Dockerfile\n9:127:A worker's inputs are `.ard-input/<issue#>/issue.md`, `comments.md` and, on a fix step, `test-output.log` (written by the loop, never committed) and `.ard/<issue#>/plan.md`. Nobody may change `issue.md` (only the scanner writes it, through the committer, not close-out), another role's file, any other file, or delete `plan.md`. A job that owns a `plan.md` section may add, replace in place, move or remove that section; a change to the text before the first `##` heading is allowed only when the job creates the file. Headings match exactly (case-sensitive), and `##` lines inside a fenced code block are text, not headings. A change outside the allowlist fails the job as `needs-human`: the comment names up to three offending paths, and only the redacted log is committed, never the offending files. A job with no valid role file still fails as `failed`, because the allowlist is checked after the role file parses. `logs/` is the controller's: files an agent writes there are ignored, not committed. `costs/` is the controller's too, but stricter: no role may write it, so an agent write there breaks the allowlist like any other path and fails the job as `needs-human`; the controller stages its own `costs/<job-id>.json` after that check, and it is never on `closeout.WritableFor`. The allowlist is code (`closeout.WritableFor`), not config; `plan_section` only names the heading a role owns. Workers and reviewers get their inputs outside `.ard/<issue#>/` (for example `.ard-input/<issue#>/`), because anything they write under it counts as their change. `issue.md` is the issue body without ard's cost block (see Guardrails), so the table never reaches an agent; the reviewer's untrusted `.ard/<issue#>/` input includes `costs/*.json`, which is controller-written and holds no free text.\n12:166:## Scanners\n52:422:Anything unset takes its default: intake in `label` mode with `ard:pending`, scanners every 4 h with `max_open` 5 and `group_size` 10, triage every 15 min, a 30-minute job timeout, `make test`, 2 test-fix attempts and 3 review rounds. Durations accept `m`, `h` and `d`. A sidecar `repo` must be `owner/name` and its `ref` a valid git ref name (no `