eBody` that, outside fenced code blocks and inline code spans, defuses `@name` mentions (same fullwidth rule) and escapes raw `<` that begins an HTML tag or comment (`&lt;`). Leave markdown links and `<details>` that ard itself writes untouched (it only touches the scanner's `Body`). Keep fenced blocks verbatim except that `<!--`/`-->` are already handled by `neutralize`.\n4. `internal/roles/scanners/docs/docscan.go:340`: this program is stdlib-only and built standalone, so it cannot import `internal/scanner`. Keep its own `code()` but strengthen it to the same rule: replace backtick with `'`, drop control characters, replace `<`, `>` with `‹`, `›`, and `@` with `＠`. Use it for every path or identifier written into a title or body (`docscan.go:385`, `:426`, and any title built from `pk.name` or a directory name; grep `Title:` in the file and wrap).\n5. `internal/roles/scanners/error-codes/errcodes.jq:97`: add `def code: ...` (same rule as step 4, jq `gsub`) next to `safe`, build the title as `(.key | code) + \" \" + $title`, and use `code` for the paths in `locs` (`:89`); the body already uses a `text` fence, so only escape a fence-closing triple backtick as the cve scanner does.\n6. `internal/roles/scanners/cve/merge.jq:128-150`: extend `safetxt` to also map `@` to `＠`, and apply `safetxt` to `$pkg` in the title (`:145`; it currently removes only backticks and newlines, not `<`, `>`, `@`) and to `$m`. The identical copy `.ard/scanners/cve/merge.jq` is a protected path and is not touched (see Risk).\n7. `docs/proposal.md` (Scanners section, after \"The output schema is strict\"): add a paragraph \"**Scanner text is untrusted.**\" stating: the controller neutralises every title centrally (control characters collapsed, backtick, `<`, `>`, `@` mention and link brackets defused, comment delimiters escaped, length capped) before filing or editing; bodies are markdown, so a scanner must wrap every path or identifier it interpolates in inline code through its own `code()` helper (backtick to `'`, same rule as `detailBlock`'s file list) and must not rely on the controller for body markup; a table test with hostile input guards each starter scanner.\n8. Tests (see Test plan).\n\n### Test plan\nCommand: `make test` (check the Makefile; otherwise `go test ./...`). Targeted: `go test ./internal/scanner ./internal/roles`.\n- `internal/scanner/marker_test.go`, `TestSafeTitle` (table): `` a`b `` gives `a'b`; `<img src=x onerror=1>` has no `<` or `>`; `<!-- x -->` has no `<!--`; `hi @octocat` has no `@octocat` match; `x@y.com` unchanged apart from no-mention rule (email stays readable); `a\\nb\\tc\\x00d` is one line, single spaces, no control characters; `[x](http://e)` is no live link; empty after cleaning stays non-empty fallback (return the scanner name in `IssueTitle`); idempotent (`SafeTitle(SafeTitle(s)) == SafeTitle(s)`); 400 `é` still cut to `MaxTitleChars` runes without splitting.\n- `TestIssueTitle` existing cases still pass; add a hostile group title case.\n- `TestDetailBlockHostile`: hostile `Title`, `Files`, `Body` yield no live `<img`, no `@octocat`, no `<!--` outside ard's own markers (assert `ParseMarkers`/`ParseLines` round-trip still finds only the real ones).\n- `internal/roles/docs_test.go`, `errcodes_test.go`, `cve_test.go`: table over hostile repo paths and identifiers (a backtick, `<img>`, `@octocat`, `<!--`) for each starter scanner; run the scanner, then assert every emitted `title`, `body` and `files` entry, passed through `scanner.IssueTitle`/`detailBlock`, matches none of: a raw backtick inside a code span, `<img`, `<!--`, `@octocat`. Follow how those files already build fixture repos and skip the same way the integration tests do when jq or Docker are missing.\n- Failure case: a scanner emitting a title with a control character still fails `validateFinding` (unchanged).\n\n### Risk\nMedium. Titles are part of near-duplicate detection and marker lines, so changing them alters existing issues' text on the next edit;